  "correction_rules": [
    "Reduce forecast overshoots following positive sentiment spikes (e.g., sentiment > 0.00) by 5-15% to avoid overreaction.",
    "Adjust downward forecasts when sentiment is negative (e.g., sentiment < 0.00) by 5-10% to account for bearish momentum.",
    "Apply mean reversion bias: if forecast deviates > 10% from recent 5-day average, adjust toward historical mean.",
    "Correct for lagged overestimation: if true outcome is lower than forecast by > 5% and sentiment is neutral, reduce next forecast by 3-5%.",
    "When sentiment is volatile (e.g., alternating +/– 0.20), dampen forecast volatility by smoothing with 3-day moving average.",
    "For long-term (30d) forecasts, cap maximum upward deviation at +10% above recent 15-day high to prevent runaway spikes."
  ]
}
